// REJECTS: Unexpected token ']'. Valid alternatives: ['TDS']
//
// `serviceOutputTargets: ... BRACKET_OPEN serviceOutputTarget (COMMA serviceOutputTarget)*
// BRACKET_CLOSE ...` -- no `?` around the group, so the list must have at least one entry.
//
// This is the odd one out among the bracketed lists in this grammar: `keys: []`,
// `partitionFields: []`, `deleteValues: []` (v2), `tests: []` and `testBatches: []` are all
// wrapped in `( ... )?` and may be empty. Only this one may not, and nothing marks it as
// special except the missing question mark.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::EmptyServiceOutputTargets
{
  doc: 'an empty service output target list';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  serviceOutputTargets:
  [
  ];
}
